⍝ D-95: a dfn naming ⍺⍺ is a monadic operator, one naming ⍵⍵ a dyadic one
🍎> +{⍺⍺/⍵}1 2 3
⍝ expect: 6
🍎> ×{⍵⍵ ⍺⍺ ⍵}- 3
⍝ expect: ¯1
🍎> 2 +{⍺ ⍺⍺ ⍵} 3
⍝ expect: 5
🍎> R←{⍺⍺/⍵}
🍎> +R 1 2 3
⍝ expect: 6
🍎> ×R 1 2 3 4
⍝ expect: 24
🍎> TW←{⍺⍺ ⍺⍺ ⍵}
🍎> {⍵+1}TW 5
⍝ expect: 7
🍎> D←{⍺⍺ ⍵⍵ ⍵}
🍎> ⌽D⍳ 3
⍝ expect: 3 2 1
🍎> DIV←{⍺÷⍵}
🍎> 1 DIV{⍺ ⍺⍺ ⍵}4
⍝ expect: 0.25
⍝ array operands:  an array to the left, and an array to the right of a dyadic operator
🍎> 2 {⍺⍺+⍵} 3
⍝ expect: 5
🍎> (1 2) {⍺⍺×⍵} 3
⍝ expect: 3 6
🍎> K←10
🍎> K {⍺⍺-⍵} 3
⍝ expect: 7
🍎> P←{⍺⍺*⍵}
🍎> 2 P 3
⍝ expect: 8
🍎> +{⍺⍺/⍵⍵↑⍵}2 ⍳5
⍝ expect: 3
🍎> ×{⍵⍵ ⍺⍺ ⍵}10⊢5
⍝ expect: 50
⍝ ∇∇ is the operator itself; ∇ inside an operator keeps its operands
🍎> C←{⍵≤0: ⍺⍺ 100 ⋄ ⍺⍺ ∇∇ ⍵-1}
🍎> ÷C 3
⍝ expect: 0.01
🍎> E←{⍵≤0: ⍺⍺ 4 ⋄ ∇ ⍵-1}
🍎> ÷E 3
⍝ expect: 0.25
🍎> S←{⍵≤1: ⍺⍺ ⍵ ⋄ (⍺⍺ ∇∇ ⍵-1)+⍺⍺ ∇∇ ⍵-2}
🍎> ⊢S 10
⍝ expect: 55
⍝ a local dfn as the operand of a named operator
🍎> W←{G←{⍵×10} ⋄ G C ⍵}
🍎> W 2
⍝ expect: 1000
🍎> {⍺⍺/⍵} 1 2
⍝ refuse: %syntax-error
